## Telegram Bot Token Rotation — Zero Downtime

**Mode confirmed:** Long-polling (no webhook). Telegram queues messages server-side during the restart gap (~15 seconds), so nothing is lost.

---

### Step 1 — Revoke in BotFather (start the clock here)

Message `@BotFather` → `/mybots` → `@Maddieprop_bot` → `API Token` → `Revoke current token`. Copy the new token immediately — **complete steps 2–3 within 60 seconds**.

### Step 2 — Update the env file

```bash
nano /Users/winfredquek/.telegram-bot.env
```

Replace `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` value only. No other lines. Verify no trailing whitespace.

### Step 3 — Kick the daemon (atomic kill + relaunch)

```bash
launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.crestbrick.telegram-bot
```

The `-k` flag kills the live process and immediately spawns a fresh one that reads the new token. No plist unload/reload needed.

### Step 4 — Verify

```bash
tail -5 /Users/winfredquek/.telegram-bot/bot.log
bash /Users/winfredquek/.claude/bin/telegram-heartbeat.sh && tail -1 /Users/winfredquek/.claude/bin/telegram-heartbeat.log
```

Expected: `Bot started. Polling as @Maddieprop_bot...` and `Telegram OK`.

### Step 5 — Clear watchdog state

```bash
: > /Users/winfredquek/.claude/state/telegram-bot-restart.attempts
: > /Users/winfredquek/.claude/state/telegram-bot-restart.state
```

---

### Key facts

| Fact | Detail |
|---|---|
| Token stored | `/Users/winfredquek/.telegram-bot.env` (perms 600 — correct) |
| Token loaded | Once at startup (`_ENV_CACHE`) — requires process restart |
| Watchdog | Sources the env file fresh each run — auto-picks up new token |
| Heartbeat | Runs daily at 09:00, reads env directly — no intervention needed |
| Webhook | None registered — no `setWebhook` call required |
| `BOT_ID` / `BOT_USERNAME` | Unchanged on rotation — leave them as-is |

One cleanup flag: `bot.py` is currently `750` (world-execute). Worth tightening with `chmod 700 /Users/winfredquek/.telegram-bot/bot.py` while you're in there.


